{"id": "EUVD-2026-86971", "enisaUuid": "6cba843a-dd77-3f1f-8895-b9a660a58f18", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nntfs: fix kmap_local leak in write_mft_record_nolock() error paths\n\nwrite_mft_record_nolock() maps the MFT record folio with\nkmap_local_folio(), but the pre_write_mst_fixup() and\nbio_add_folio() failure paths jump to the error label without\nunmapping it. kmap_local mappings are stack-ordered per task, so\nleaking one corrupts the nesting for any outer mapping.\n\nUnmap the folio on those error paths too.", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:36:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:33", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5d7f7bf8fba8cf563b42b44aa4ab3d9928ac480c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cf06dcd572845723821b54a608fc2da995c3c8e2"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5q4f-hqwh-q345", "CVE-2026-98140"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.15, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "422ac46e-bb00-326d-a2a6-1e7230934f62", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "115380f9a2f9675c7924563cbba70d40cae8fb81 <cf06dcd572845723821b54a608fc2da995c3c8e2"}, {"id": "83da2ac4-4c88-3109-82e2-d34f57a3cd5a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7.1"}, {"id": "ad1c2c63-de2e-3260-9fb5-1d24f452efac", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b87fa9ae-fb2a-3c2e-b40e-28daf284f405", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f34172f6-449f-3ae4-aace-f76f08797bcb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.7"}, {"id": "f93a848b-fa8b-3e31-9236-c4d711f6ae27", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "115380f9a2f9675c7924563cbba70d40cae8fb81 <5d7f7bf8fba8cf563b42b44aa4ab3d9928ac480c"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "86dceeed-7270-342f-b87e-6a0f30f69f59", "ven